{"shortDescription":"Asia fuel oil premiums softened on Thursday, while timespreads traded lower versus the previous close for both 380-cst high sulphur fuel oil (HSFO) and very low sulphur fuel oil (VLSFO).Cash differentials for both grades were pegged at weaker premiums over cargo quotes, with physical trades emergin…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Asia fuel oil premiums softened on Thursday, while timespreads traded lower versus the previous close for both 380-cst high sulphur fuel oil (HSFO) and very low sulphur fuel oil (VLSFO)."]},{"type":"p","children":["Cash differentials for both grades were pegged at weaker premiums over cargo quotes, with physical trades emerging at lower values for several October loading dates."]},{"type":"p","children":["While the premiums have pared back after a jump that took place following recent Middle Eastern escalations, some fuel oil traders said supply uncertainties for Q4 would continue to keep a floor on price benchmarks."]},{"type":"p","children":["The market continues to monitor regional sale tenders for some supply relief."]},{"type":"p","children":["Indonesia's Pertamina offered 100,000 barrels of marine fuel oil for loading from Cilacap between September 30 and October 1, according to market sources. Meanwhile, India's IOC offered 27,500 tons of HSFO for loading from Chennai between October 4 and 8. Both tenders closed on Thursday."]},{"type":"p","children":["Separately, spot demand for marine fuel has slowed in recent sessions amid volatile swings in upstream Brent prices this week, several bunker suppliers said. Delivered premiums for Singapore VLSFO have eased slightly, though holding above $50 a ton for prompt dates."]},{"type":"p","children":["Meanwhile, cracks for HSFO and VLSFO diverged in direction on Thursday, LSEG data showed."]},{"type":"p","children":["The October VLSFO/Brent crack (LFO05SGBRTCMc1) inched higher day-on-day to a premium near $23.15 a barrel at the Asia close (0830 GMT). In contrast, the 380-cst HSFO crack (FO380BRTCKMc1) sold off to close at a discount that as wider than $3 a barrel."]},{"type":"p","children":["INVENTORY DATA"]},{"type":"p","children":["Singapore's residual fuel stockpiles (STKRS-SIN) dipped 1.0% week-on-week to 20.14 million barrels (3.17 million tons) in the week to September 16, latest Enterprise Singapore data showed on Thursday."]},{"type":"p","children":["Despite the slight decline, the inventories averaged higher this month versus last month's 18.6 million barrels per week."]},{"type":"p","children":["OTHER NEWS"]},{"type":"p","children":["- Oil prices eased on Thursday, extending losses as reports of additional Saudi crude cargoes through Oman eased supply concerns, though prices stayed above $100 a barrel on fears the Middle East conflict could widen."]},{"type":"p","children":["- A Ukrainian drone attack damaged an oil refinery in the Russian city of Yaroslavl, causing a fire that was later doused, regional Governor Mikhail Yevrayev said on Thursday on the Telegram messaging app."]},{"type":"p","children":["- India has warned Washington that new measures to levy tariffs over the purchase of Russian oil could impact bilateral ties, the South Asian nation's foreign ministry said on Thursday, hours after the U.S. made a new move to punish such buyers."]},{"type":"p","children":["- A fresh rally in international diesel prices has widened the gap between international prices and Brazil's state-owned oil company Petrobras to record levels, prompting independent importers to delay purchases, industry executives told Reuters."]},{"type":"p","children":["WINDOW TRADES"]},{"type":"p","children":["- 180-cst HSFO: No trade."]},{"type":"p","children":["- 380-cst HSFO: Five trades."]},{"type":"p","children":["- 0.5% VLSFO: One trade."]},{"type":"p","children":["ASSESSMENTS"]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children